cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Bistable Fit Bench"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Jacquin
    given-names: Valentin
repository-code: "https://github.com/valjcq/bistable_bench_llm_fit"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic environment and benchmark for fitting multistable (bistable) neural rate models,
  built to test whether an LLM agent adds anything over a fixed expert optimization pipeline. On
  these tasks a well-designed loss does most of the solving; a local open model matched the fixed
  pipeline on solvable tasks but claimed solutions on 46 of 287 provably impossible-task episodes,
  against 0 of 72 for the pipeline.
